<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρούρ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, poet. Noun: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>that which is watched</i> or <i>guarded,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λείας βουκόλων φρουρήματα</span> the
			herdsmen's <i>charge</i> of spoil, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				54
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>guard,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				706
			</span></i>; of a single man, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Th.</u>
				449
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγχαι δεσποτῶν φρουρήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					798
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>watch, ward,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρούρημα ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ion</u>
					511
				</span></i>
			 (troch.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
